<description>
Copy the red template sprite along the control-pixel line, preserving control gaps and recoloring each copy.

Input structure
The grid has a black background, one 8-connected red template sprite, and
several isolated control pixels in one row or column.  Exactly one control
pixel has the template color.

Rule
Read the control pixels left-to-right or top-to-bottom.  The copy matching
the template-color control is the original sprite; each neighboring control
becomes a same-shape copy in that control color.  The empty cells between
adjacent control pixels become the empty columns or rows between adjacent
sprite bboxes.

Key insight
The singleton control line is a compressed ordered layout: expanding each
marker to the template bbox while keeping the inter-marker gaps fixes every
copy position from the original sprite.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "isolated control pixels s in the single row or column, ordered left-to-right or top-to-bottom",
  "dst": "expanded sprite-copy slots d along the same axis, with the template-color slot fixed at the original red sprite bbox",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) == rank(d); empty gaps between adjacent controls become gaps between adjacent sprite bboxes",
  "transform": "stamp the 8-connected red sprite mask into each slot recolored to s.color; keep control pixels and the original template unchanged",
  "symbol_instructions": "the control-pixel line gives the copy colors, read direction, and inter-copy gaps"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-23 rows x 14-24 cols, black background
  sprite:
    shape: 3x3 bbox, 8-connected, monochromatic [observed]
    area: 6-7 cells (density 0.67-0.78)
    color: 2 (red) [observed]
    no_symmetry_required: true
  control_line:
    count: 4-5 isolated single pixels sharing one row or one column
    axis: horizontal (same row) or vertical (same col)
    position: near grid edge, row/col 1-2 [observed]
    separation_from_copies: control line row/col does not overlap sprite copy rows/cols (>=5 apart)
    ordering: sorted left-to-right (horiz) or top-to-bottom (vert)
    colors: 2-4 distinct non-bg colors; exactly one pixel has the sprite color (anchor)
    color_repeats: allowed (non-anchor colors may repeat)
    gaps: 1-4 empty cells between consecutive control positions
  layout:
    anchor_control: marks position of original sprite; copies expand from it
    each_copy: sprite mask recolored to corresponding control pixel color
    inter-copy_gap: equals gap between corresponding consecutive control pixels
    all_copies_in_bounds: required
    copies_span: >=75% of expansion axis [observed]
  output:
    same grid size; stamp recolored copies at computed positions; controls and original sprite persist

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (13-23 x 14-24) and expansion axis (horizontal or vertical).
    2. Design a 3x3 sprite mask (6-7 cells, 8-connected) in color 2.
    3. Choose N=4-5 control colors (exactly one is color 2, others from non-bg palette, repeats ok).
    4. Choose N-1 inter-copy gaps (each 1-4). Compute total expansion span = N*3 + sum(gaps).
       Verify span fits in grid with >=0 margin on each side.
    5. Place copies along expansion axis starting from a random valid offset.
       Record each copy start position and color. Stamp all copies into the output grid.
    6. Place the control line on a row/col near the opposite edge (row/col 1-2), not overlapping copy rows/cols.
       Compute control positions from copy starts by reversing the expansion formula
       (anchor position = any valid position; others spaced by sprite_size + gap).
    7. To produce the input, start from the output, erase all non-anchor copies (set to bg),
       keep the anchor copy (original sprite) and all control pixels.
```
